{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794532193447,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5322ffeAAux2z5sLfP46J","part":{"id":"prt_1d27434a7001c9ipZK9dQVCQNT","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5322ffeAAux2z5sLfP46J","messageID":"msg_1d2742d4a001GLaCKipC0MbQdz","type":"step-start","snapshot":"a0b6bdf91b41682d39d1c5c5b2d2f7c0f8089aca"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794532195397,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5322ffeAAux2z5sLfP46J","part":{"partID":"prt_1d274387e002T619fyOyvzt6QS","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5322ffeAAux2z5sLfP46J","messageID":"msg_1d2742d4a001GLaCKipC0MbQdz","type":"tool","id":"call_4890e51652864f329f3da726","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/utils/workspace-root.ts"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/utils/workspace-root.ts, lines 1-132\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Advisor Workspace Root Walk-Up\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: // Shared walk-up helper used by every advisor handler, daemon, bench,\n5: // and parity test that needs to resolve the workspace root from a\n6: // runtime-supplied starting directory. Mirrors the `code_graph/lib/utils/\n7: // workspace-path.ts` shape: one canonicalized helper, parametrizable by\n8: // start dir, depth cap, and sentinel path.\n9: \n10: import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';\n11: import { resolve, sep } from 'node:path';\n12: \n13: export interface AdvisorWorkspaceRootOptions {\n14:   readonly maxDepth?: number;\n15:   readonly sentinel?: string;\n16: }\n17: \n18: const DEFAULT_MAX_DEPTH = 14;\n19: // The source tree sits under `.skilled` or `.opencode`, and a checkout may link one\n20: // name to the other, so both names mark the same tree. A sentinel that starts with\n21: // either name is tested under each, and the fallback hoists above either.\n22: const SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES: readonly string[] = ['.skilled', '.opencode'];\n23: // Strict sentinel: anchors on the canonical SKILL.md inside system-spec-kit so\n24: // nested mock dirs (e.g. runtime/.opencode/skills/.state/advisor/) cannot\n25: // satisfy the walk-up. A bare `.opencode/skills` directory is trivially\n26: // self-perpetuating: once any caller writes anything under it from a wrong\n27: // cwd, the walk-up resolver returns that wrong cwd on subsequent calls.\n28: // `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:detectRepoRoot` uses the same strict\n29: // sentinel for the same reason — keep these two in lockstep.\n30: const DEFAULT_SENTINEL = '.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md';\n31: \n32: /**\n33:  * Spell a sentinel under every source-root name when its first segment is one. The\n34:  * legacy spec alias keeps its one `.opencode/specs` spelling, so a sentinel under it\n35:  * is tested as written. A sentinel spelled under `.skilled/specs` still tests that\n36:  * legacy spelling, because it is the only one the alias has.\n37:  */\n38: function sentinelSpellings(sentinel: string): string[] {\n39:   const [head, ...rest] = sentinel.split('/');\n40:   if (rest.length === 0 || !SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(head) || (head === '.opencode' && rest[0] === 'specs')) return [sentinel];\n41:   return SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.map((name) => [name, ...rest].join('/'));\n42: }\n43: \n44: /**\n45:  * When the sentinel walk-up fails, the resolver must never hand back a\n46:  * directory that sits *inside* a source tree. The advisor writes runtime\n47:  * state under whatever root this returns, so a root inside `.opencode/` would\n48:  * materialize a nested `.opencode/skills/...` tree there on every run — and that\n49:  * nested tree then satisfies future walk-ups, making the leak permanent.\n50:  *\n51:  * The rule is structural rather than an enumeration of known-bad subtrees: a\n52:  * `.skilled/` or `.opencode/` directory is by definition a child of the workspace\n53:  * root, so any candidate containing either path segment is provably not the root.\n54:  * Hoisting above the OUTERMOST such segment yields the real root.\n55:  *\n56:  * An earlier version listed `specs/` only. That shape could not protect subtrees\n57:  * nobody had thought of, and leaks into `skills/` continued unnoticed because\n58:  * neither the guard nor its test considered them.\n59:  *\n60:  * Returns null when `dir` is not inside a `.skilled` or `.opencode` tree.\n61:  */\n62: function hoistAboveOpencodeTree(dir: string): string | null {\n63:   const parts = resolve(dir).split(sep);\n64:   // Outermost wins: a leak can nest several levels deep, and hoisting to the\n65:   // innermost source-root segment would land inside the real tree.\n66:   for (let index = 1; index < parts.length; index += 1) {\n67:     if (SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(parts[index])) {\n68:       return parts.slice(0, index).join(sep) || sep;\n69:     }\n70:   }\n71:   return null;\n72: }\n73: \n74: /**\n75:  * A walk capped below the root never reaches the sentinel, yet the root is still the\n76:  * start itself or the parent of one source-root segment in the start path. Testing the\n77:  * start, then those parents nearest first, as the walk would, keeps a workspace that\n78:  * sits under a directory named `.skilled` or `.opencode` instead of hoisting past it.\n79:  * Returns null when none of them holds the sentinel.\n80:  */\n81: function nearestSentinelHolder(dir: string, sentinels: readonly string[]): string | null {\n82:   const holdsSentinel = (candidate: string): boolean => sentinels.some((sentinel) => existsSync(resolve(candidate, sentinel)));\n83:   if (holdsSentinel(dir)) return resolve(dir);\n84:   const parts = resolve(dir).split(sep);\n85:   for (let index = parts.length - 1; index >= 1; index -= 1) {\n86:     if (!SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(parts[index])) continue;\n87:     const parent = parts.slice(0, index).join(sep) || sep;\n88:     if (holdsSentinel(parent)) return parent;\n89:   }\n90:   return null;\n91: }\n92: \n93: /**\n94:  * Walk up parent directories from `start` until the `sentinel` path is found\n95:  * relative to the candidate directory. Returns the first directory that\n96:  * contains `sentinel`. If no candidate is found within `maxDepth` iterations,\n97:  * the start or the nearest source-root parent in its path that holds the\n98:  * sentinel is the root. Failing that, the result is the directory above the\n99:  * outermost source-root segment in `start`, and a `start` outside any source\n100:  * tree comes back canonicalized.\n101:  *\n102:  * The default sentinel is the canonical `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md`\n103:  * file rather than a bare `.opencode/skills` directory. Bare-directory sentinels\n104:  * are vulnerable to self-perpetuation: a buggy caller writing to\n105:  * `<wrong-cwd>/.opencode/skills/...` creates a directory that satisfies the\n106:  * sentinel check on every subsequent walk-up, so the resolver returns the\n107:  * wrong cwd forever. Anchoring on a real authored file in the canonical skill\n108:  * removes that footgun.\n109:  *\n110:  * @param start - The directory to start walking from. Defaults to `process.cwd()`.\n111:  * @param opts.maxDepth - Maximum number of parent steps to walk. Defaults to 14.\n112:  * @param opts.sentinel - Path (relative to a candidate directory) used as the\n113:  *   workspace marker. Defaults to `'.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md'`.\n114:  */\n115: export function findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot(\n116:   start: string = process.cwd(),\n117:   opts: AdvisorWorkspaceRootOptions = {},\n118: ): string {\n119:   const maxDepth = opts.maxDepth ?? DEFAULT_MAX_DEPTH;\n120:   const sentinels = sentinelSpellings(opts.sentinel ?? DEFAULT_SENTINEL);\n121:   let current = resolve(start);\n122:   for (let index = 0; index < maxDepth; index += 1) {\n123:     if (sentinels.some((sentinel) => existsSync(resolve(current, sentinel)))) return current;\n124:     const parent = resolve(current, '..');\n125:     if (parent === current) break;\n126:     current = parent;\n127:   }\n128:   // Sentinel not found within maxDepth. Never fall back to a path inside a\n129:   // source tree — that is provably not a workspace root, and writing state\n130:   // there creates a nested tree that re-anchors every future walk-up.\n131:   return nearestSentinelHolder(start, sentinels) ?? hoistAboveOpencodeTree(start) ?? resolve(start);\n132: }","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/utils/workspace-root.ts, lines 1-132\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Advisor Workspace Root Walk-Up\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: // Shared walk-up helper used by every advisor handler, daemon, bench,\n5: // and parity test that needs to resolve the workspace root from a\n6: // runtime-supplied starting directory. Mirrors the `code_graph/lib/utils/\n7: // workspace-path.ts` shape: one canonicalized helper, parametrizable by\n8: // start dir, depth cap, and sentinel path.\n9: \n10: import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';\n11: import { resolve, sep } from 'node:path';\n12: \n13: export interface AdvisorWorkspaceRootOptions {\n14:   readonly maxDepth?: number;\n15:   readonly sentinel?: string;\n16: }\n17: \n18: const DEFAULT_MAX_DEPTH = 14;\n19: // The source tree sits under `.skilled` or `.opencode`, and a checkout may link one\n20: // name to the other, so both names mark the same tree. A sentinel that starts with\n21: // either name is tested under each, and the fallback hoists above either.\n22: const SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES: readonly string[] = ['.skilled', '.opencode'];\n23: // Strict sentinel: anchors on the canonical SKILL.md inside system-spec-kit so\n24: // nested mock dirs (e.g. runtime/.opencode/skills/.state/advisor/) cannot\n25: // satisfy the walk-up. A bare `.opencode/skills` directory is trivially\n26: // self-perpetuating: once any caller writes anything under it from a wrong\n27: // cwd, the walk-up resolver returns that wrong cwd on subsequent calls.\n28: // `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:detectRepoRoot` uses the same strict\n29: // sentinel for the same reason — keep these two in lockstep.\n30: const DEFAULT_SENTINEL = '.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md';\n31: \n32: /**\n33:  * Spell a sentinel under every source-root name when its first segment is one. The\n34:  * legacy spec alias keeps its one `.opencode/specs` spelling, so a sentinel under it\n35:  * is tested as written. A sentinel spelled under `.skilled/specs` still tests that\n36:  * legacy spelling, because it is the only one the alias has.\n37:  */\n38: function sentinelSpellings(sentinel: string): string[] {\n39:   const [head, ...rest] = sentinel.split('/');\n40:   if (rest.length === 0 || !SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(head) || (head === '.opencode' && rest[0] === 'specs')) return [sentinel];\n41:   return SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.map((name) => [name, ...rest].join('/'));\n42: }\n43: \n44: /**\n45:  * When the sentinel walk-up fails, the resolver must never hand back a\n46:  * directory that sits *inside* a source tree. The advisor writes runtime\n47:  * state under whatever root this returns, so a root inside `.opencode/` would\n48:  * materialize a nested `.opencode/skills/...` tree there on every run — and that\n49:  * nested tree then satisfies future walk-ups, making the leak permanent.\n50:  *\n51:  * The rule is structural rather than an enumeration of known-bad subtrees: a\n52:  * `.skilled/` or `.opencode/` directory is by definition a child of the workspace\n53:  * root, so any candidate containing either path segment is provably not the root.\n54:  * Hoisting above the OUTERMOST such segment yields the real root.\n55:  *\n56:  * An earlier version listed `specs/` only. That shape could not protect subtrees\n57:  * nobody had thought of, and leaks into `skills/` continued unnoticed because\n58:  * neither the guard nor its test considered them.\n59:  *\n60:  * Returns null when `dir` is not inside a `.skilled` or `.opencode` tree.\n61:  */\n62: function hoistAboveOpencodeTree(dir: string): string | null {\n63:   const parts = resolve(dir).split(sep);\n64:   // Outermost wins: a leak can nest several levels deep, and hoisting to the\n65:   // innermost source-root segment would land inside the real tree.\n66:   for (let index = 1; index < parts.length; index += 1) {\n67:     if (SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(parts[index])) {\n68:       return parts.slice(0, index).join(sep) || sep;\n69:     }\n70:   }\n71:   return null;\n72: }\n73: \n74: /**\n75:  * A walk capped below the root never reaches the sentinel, yet the root is still the\n76:  * start itself or the parent of one source-root segment in the start path. Testing the\n77:  * start, then those parents nearest first, as the walk would, keeps a workspace that\n78:  * sits under a directory named `.skilled` or `.opencode` instead of hoisting past it.\n79:  * Returns null when none of them holds the sentinel.\n80:  */\n81: function nearestSentinelHolder(dir: string, sentinels: readonly string[]): string | null {\n82:   const holdsSentinel = (candidate: string): boolean => sentinels.some((sentinel) => existsSync(resolve(candidate, sentinel)));\n83:   if (holdsSentinel(dir)) return resolve(dir);\n84:   const parts = resolve(dir).split(sep);\n85:   for (let index = parts.length - 1; index >= 1; index -= 1) {\n86:     if (!SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(parts[index])) continue;\n87:     const parent = parts.slice(0, index).join(sep) || sep;\n88:     if (holdsSentinel(parent)) return parent;\n89:   }\n90:   return null;\n91: }\n92: \n93: /**\n94:  * Walk up parent directories from `start` until the `sentinel` path is found\n95:  * relative to the candidate directory. Returns the first directory that\n96:  * contains `sentinel`. If no candidate is found within `maxDepth` iterations,\n97:  * the start or the nearest source-root parent in its path that holds the\n98:  * sentinel is the root. Failing that, the result is the directory above the\n99:  * outermost source-root segment in `start`, and a `start` outside any source\n100:  * tree comes back canonicalized.\n101:  *\n102:  * The default sentinel is the canonical `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md`\n103:  * file rather than a bare `.opencode/skills` directory. Bare-directory sentinels\n104:  * are vulnerable to self-perpetuation: a buggy caller writing to\n105:  * `<wrong-cwd>/.opencode/skills/...` creates a directory that satisfies the\n106:  * sentinel check on every subsequent walk-up, so the resolver returns the\n107:  * wrong cwd forever. Anchoring on a real authored file in the canonical skill\n108:  * removes that footgun.\n109:  *\n110:  * @param start - The directory to start walking from. Defaults to `process.cwd()`.\n111:  * @param opts.maxDepth - Maximum number of parent steps to walk. Defaults to 14.\n112:  * @param opts.sentinel - Path (relative to a candidate directory) used as the\n113:  *   workspace marker. Defaults to `'.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md'`.\n114:  */\n115: export function findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot(\n116:   start: string = process.cwd(),\n117:   opts: AdvisorWorkspaceRootOptions = {},\n118: ): string {\n119:   const maxDepth = opts.maxDepth ?? DEFAULT_MAX_DEPTH;\n120:   const sentinels = sentinelSpellings(opts.sentinel ?? DEFAULT_SENTINEL);\n121:   let current = resolve(start);\n122:   for (let index = 0; index < maxDepth; index += 1) {\n123:     if (sentinels.some((sentinel) => existsSync(resolve(current, sentinel)))) return current;\n124:     const parent = resolve(current, '..');\n125:     if (parent === current) break;\n126:     current = parent;\n127:   }\n128:   // Sentinel not found within maxDepth. Never fall back to a path inside a\n129:   // source tree — that is provably not a workspace root, and writing state\n130:   // there creates a nested tree that re-anchors every future walk-up.\n131:   return nearestSentinelHolder(start, sentinels) ?? hoistAboveOpencodeTree(start) ?? resolve(start);\n132: }"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/utils/workspace-root.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794532194430,"end":1794532195397}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794532195401,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5322ffeAAux2z5sLfP46J","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2743a14001jIkwegufmAVbgO","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5322ffeAAux2z5sLfP46J","messageID":"msg_1d2742d4a001GLaCKipC0MbQdz","type":"tool","id":"call_f8f5cfd44f484528bb561b25","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md","offset":60,"limit":45},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 60-104\n60: \n61: The ambiguous head applies the same label to both sides: `Advisor: <freshness>; ambiguous: <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> vs <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` Each label part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`, so a control character, a line break or an instruction-shaped label renders nothing rather than reaching the model. The `Also:` line still names a doctor command by its runnable string.\n62: \n63: ### Degraded contract\n64: \n65: When the daemon is unreachable, the CLI runs the local Python scorer and returns `status: ok` with `degraded: true` and `source: local-scorer`. The local scorer returns command row ids, which a reader cannot type, so the CLI rewrites each row before the brief renders:\n66: \n67: - A row whose bare slash command appears in the prompt (the row's `command` text before the first space) keeps its command fields: `skillId` is the row id, `kind` is `command`, `command` is the runnable string, `policy` is present when the row has one and `ownerSkillId` names the owning skill. A typed `/speckit:save this session` renders `system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start)`.\n68: - Every other row collapses to its owner skill: `skillId` is `ownerSkillId` and `kind` is `skill`. It is dropped when that skill is already offered, so the degraded brief never repeats a skill.\n69: \n70: Rows below the threshold are discarded before either rule applies. The degraded brief therefore keeps the same head form and names a skill that exists rather than a raw row id.\n71: \n72: ---\n73: \n74: ## 3. PER-RUNTIME DELIVERY\n75: \n76: Every native runtime and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`. The OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. The native adapters differ in prompt event, transport and delivery channel.\n77: \n78: | Runtime | Adapter | Event / wiring | Payload difference it handles | Delivery |\n79: |---|---|---|---|---|\n80: | **Claude** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `system-skill-advisor/.../dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.claude/settings.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 3s | Shim resolves the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor (install-anchored, not CWD-relative). Bounded stdin (1 MiB), bounded child stdio, 2.5s child timeout, `SIGKILL` on timeout | `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON on stdout. `{}` on any failure |\n81: | **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n82: | **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n83: | **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n84: | **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, re-exported by its one-line `.pi/extensions/` entry) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n85: | **OpenCode** | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Plugin, loaded by OpenCode's flat glob over `.opencode/plugins/`. `experimental.chat.system.transform` per prompt, `event` for session lifecycle, `tool` for status | Shells out to the advisor CLI (bounded timeout, stdout cap 256 KiB, grace termination), TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, transform-dedup integration | Brief appended to `output.system`. `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` tool returns a key=value report (no raw path leakage) |\n86: | **DSH** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` | `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false` | Proxies the latest operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `dsh`. A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief | Brief added to the step |\n87: \n88: OpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n93: \n94: ```text\n95: system-skill-advisor/hooks/\n96: +-- skill-advisor-hook.md            # this reference (symlinked from .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/README.md)\n97: +-- skill-advisor-hook-validation.md # validation/audit detail\n98: +-- claude/\n99: |   +-- README.md\n100: |   +-- directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts\n101: |   `-- user-prompt-submit.ts         # real advisor handler (Claude shape)\n102: +-- dsh/\n103: |   +-- README.md\n104: |   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real DSH adapter (.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ imports it)\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 105]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 60-104\n60: \n61: The ambiguous head applies the same label to both sides: `Advisor: <freshness>; ambiguous: <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> vs <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` Each label part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`, so a control character, a line break or an instruction-shaped label renders nothing rather than reaching the model. The `Also:` line still names a doctor command by its runnable string.\n62: \n63: ### Degraded contract\n64: \n65: When the daemon is unreachable, the CLI runs the local Python scorer and returns `status: ok` with `degraded: true` and `source: local-scorer`. The local scorer returns command row ids, which a reader cannot type, so the CLI rewrites each row before the brief renders:\n66: \n67: - A row whose bare slash command appears in the prompt (the row's `command` text before the first space) keeps its command fields: `skillId` is the row id, `kind` is `command`, `command` is the runnable string, `policy` is present when the row has one and `ownerSkillId` names the owning skill. A typed `/speckit:save this session` renders `system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start)`.\n68: - Every other row collapses to its owner skill: `skillId` is `ownerSkillId` and `kind` is `skill`. It is dropped when that skill is already offered, so the degraded brief never repeats a skill.\n69: \n70: Rows below the threshold are discarded before either rule applies. The degraded brief therefore keeps the same head form and names a skill that exists rather than a raw row id.\n71: \n72: ---\n73: \n74: ## 3. PER-RUNTIME DELIVERY\n75: \n76: Every native runtime and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`. The OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. The native adapters differ in prompt event, transport and delivery channel.\n77: \n78: | Runtime | Adapter | Event / wiring | Payload difference it handles | Delivery |\n79: |---|---|---|---|---|\n80: | **Claude** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `system-skill-advisor/.../dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.claude/settings.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 3s | Shim resolves the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor (install-anchored, not CWD-relative). Bounded stdin (1 MiB), bounded child stdio, 2.5s child timeout, `SIGKILL` on timeout | `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON on stdout. `{}` on any failure |\n81: | **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n82: | **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n83: | **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n84: | **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, re-exported by its one-line `.pi/extensions/` entry) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n85: | **OpenCode** | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Plugin, loaded by OpenCode's flat glob over `.opencode/plugins/`. `experimental.chat.system.transform` per prompt, `event` for session lifecycle, `tool` for status | Shells out to the advisor CLI (bounded timeout, stdout cap 256 KiB, grace termination), TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, transform-dedup integration | Brief appended to `output.system`. `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` tool returns a key=value report (no raw path leakage) |\n86: | **DSH** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` | `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false` | Proxies the latest operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `dsh`. A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief | Brief added to the step |\n87: \n88: OpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n93: \n94: ```text\n95: system-skill-advisor/hooks/\n96: +-- skill-advisor-hook.md            # this reference (symlinked from .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/README.md)\n97: +-- skill-advisor-hook-validation.md # validation/audit detail\n98: +-- claude/\n99: |   +-- README.md\n100: |   +-- directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts\n101: |   `-- user-prompt-submit.ts         # real advisor handler (Claude shape)\n102: +-- dsh/\n103: |   +-- README.md\n104: |   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real DSH adapter (.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ imports it)\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 105]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\",\"offset\":60,\"limit\":45}"},"time":{"start":1794532194836,"end":1794532195401}}}}
