{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794532203503,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5322ffeAAux2z5sLfP46J","part":{"id":"prt_1d2745bef001AODKRpL3DT77nE","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5322ffeAAux2z5sLfP46J","messageID":"msg_1d27455cb001YpZ8tuSZ3X4ATn","type":"step-start","snapshot":"765925c80f7dbbe2f26348439f5fc7f46c765a7b"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794532227690,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5322ffeAAux2z5sLfP46J","part":{"partID":"prt_1d274b5f10024Yl4tcVrW0A8L6","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5322ffeAAux2z5sLfP46J","messageID":"msg_1d27455cb001YpZ8tuSZ3X4ATn","type":"tool","id":"call_5dc54cbe8c29483b8efe49c6","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls -1 \"REPO RULES.md\" 2>/dev/null && head -60 \"REPO RULES.md\"; echo \"--- target exists?\"; ls -l .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts 2>&1; echo \"--- hooks README\"; head -30 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/README.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"REPO RULES.md\n# REPO RULES\n\nRepo-local operating rules. `AGENTS.md` **Gate 5 (§2)** makes reading this mandatory\nbefore your first write of the session; this document then routes you to every rule\nfile that governs what you are about to do. **It is a router, not a rulebook:** it\nholds no rules of its own.\n\n---\n\n## 1. HOW TO USE THIS\n\n1. **Match on the action you are about to take**, not the topic of the request.\n2. **Load before the action.** A rule read afterwards is a post-mortem.\n3. **A file already in context is not re-read.**\n4. **Every trigger that fires is loaded, not just the first.** They compose; the more\n   specific wins on conflict. Three and four firing at once is the normal case, not an\n   edge case.\n5. **Nothing fires → `AGENTS.md` alone governs.** Do not hunt for a rule to apply.\n\n### Precedence\n\n| Level | Source | Can be overridden? |\n|-------|--------|--------------------|\n| 1 | Every `AGENTS.md` §1 hard blocker, the Four Laws, PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK, Comment Hygiene, and every mandatory gate in §2 | No |\n| 2 | An explicit, in-the-moment operator instruction | Not applicable, it is the instruction |\n| 3 | These rule files, and the guidance in a skill's `SKILL.md` | Only by level 1 or 2 |\n| 4 | General judgment | By anything above |\n\nA rule file may tighten `AGENTS.md`. None relaxes a HARD BLOCK or authorizes what\n`AGENTS.md` forbids. Gate 5 does not change that: it makes the **load** mandatory,\nwhile what you load stays at level 3, the obligation to read is tier 1, the content\nis not.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TRIGGER TABLE\n\n| You are about to… | Load | It settles |\n|-------------------|------|-----------|\n| Add a file, module, class, interface, option, layer, or dependency · write a spec or plan that adds one · generalize something that works · write \"flexible\", \"future-proof\", \"scalable\", \"extensible\", \"might need\", \"best practice\", \"while we're here\" · add a test beyond the coverage floor | [`prevent-overengineering.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Whether this should exist at all, and at what size |\n| Touch a file outside the ask · fix something noticed in passing · change something else because it would make the fix easier · rename, reformat, or delete beyond the named area · deviate from an approved plan · decide what to do with the rest when part of the work is blocked · notice a defect, smell or stale comment outside the files in scope | [`scope-discipline.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | What is yours to change, and how to raise what isn't |\n| Say \"done\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", \"no regressions\" · report a result · quote a number · act on a tool's or sub-agent's success report · close out a turn · report a file path or command output · write a completion summary or tick something off as done | [`evidence-and-proof.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | What counts as proof, how a green run lies, what an honest close-out contains |\n| Decide whether to hand work to another runtime at all · hand it to a CLI executor, sub-agent, fan-out lineage, or deep loop · compose the prompt one will act on · accept or quote what one returned · answer a judgment question from your own reading alone | [`delegation-and-orchestration.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | The orchestrating posture, what a brief must carry, why one model is one opinion |\n| Delete, overwrite, migrate, deploy, publish, send, install · force-push or rewrite history · change a shared contract · touch auth, data, or config · make any call that leaves this machine · truncate · touch branches, tags, or reflogs | [`blast-radius.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Reversibility, the rollback sentence, when to stop for a yes |\n| Diagnose a failure · make a red check green · attempt the same fix twice · add a special case, retry, sleep, or broadened catch · call a failure a flake, infra, or pre-existing | [`root-cause-and-debugging.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fixing the producer instead of the symptom, and when to level up to the seam |\n| Answer without certainty · contradict the operator · fill a gap with a plausible guess · hit a contradiction between two things that must both be true · name a path, flag, function, version, or number you have not verified · not know while a plausible answer is available · see sources disagree, or the code contradict the spec, the docs or the operator · the operator asserts something you believe is wrong · change a checked answer after pushback or doubt, or drop an approach before it concludes · cite a rule, restriction, policy, limit or permission, or decline a request | [`uncertainty-and-honesty.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Confidence bands, UNKNOWN, contradiction halts |\n| Write any substantive reply, an answer, an explanation, a close-out or a status · draft or edit any sentence a reader will read · present a recommendation, a fork, or a trade-off · start a multi-step stretch of work the reader will not see inside · report what a long autonomous run found · the reader says they did not follow or asks for a plainer version | [`communication.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | How a reply reads: answer first, one recommended path, length, filler, plain sentences, punctuation, and no table in a reply |\n| End a turn · report work done, blocked, or partly done · end a turn while something you started is still running · ask the operator anything · end a turn on a fork or two acceptable paths · continue past a decision nobody made | [`communication-handoff.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | What is the operator's to do next, what is still running and what resumes it, and when a question becomes a structured choice |\n| Wire, rewire or remove a mode in a parent-hub skill · edit a hub's registry, router, root `ROUTER.md`, `graph-metadata.json` or `SKILL.md` mode table, or a mode packet's own `ROUTER.md` · report that a mode is registered, routed, reachable or integrated · quote a per-hub gate result · create a new skill under a hub, or refactor one that already lives there | [`skill-hub-routing.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | The two routing stages, what \"integrated\" requires, and checking the hub you actually changed |\n\n---\n\n## 3. INDEX\n\n| Rule | Summary |\n|------|---------|\n| [Overengineering](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Build the smallest thing that solves the stated problem; take a costlier move only by naming what fails at the cheaper one. |\n| [Scope discipline](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | The requested scope is the deliverable. Adjacent problems get named, not fixed. |\n| [Evidence and proof](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred. |\n| [Delegation and orchestration](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | Delegating makes you the orchestrator; brief with evidence, and no single model's verdict closes a question. |\n--- target exists?\nls: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts: No such file or directory\n--- hooks README\n---\ntitle: \"Skill Advisor Hook Tests\"\ndescription: \"Regression coverage for settings-driven skill advisor hook invocation shape.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"skill advisor hook tests\"\n  - \"settings driven invocation parity\"\n---\n\n# Skill Advisor Hook Tests\n\n> Regression coverage for settings-driven skill advisor hook invocation shape.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`tests/hooks/` guards the checked-in Claude settings shape used by skill advisor hook invocation.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Confirms each hook event uses the nested matcher-group shape.\n- Ensures hook commands point at `dist/hooks/claude/*` handlers.\n- Blocks accidental `hooks/copilot/` adapter references in Claude settings.\n\n---\n\n## 2. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n```text\nhooks/\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"REPO RULES.md\n# REPO RULES\n\nRepo-local operating rules. `AGENTS.md` **Gate 5 (§2)** makes reading this mandatory\nbefore your first write of the session; this document then routes you to every rule\nfile that governs what you are about to do. **It is a router, not a rulebook:** it\nholds no rules of its own.\n\n---\n\n## 1. HOW TO USE THIS\n\n1. **Match on the action you are about to take**, not the topic of the request.\n2. **Load before the action.** A rule read afterwards is a post-mortem.\n3. **A file already in context is not re-read.**\n4. **Every trigger that fires is loaded, not just the first.** They compose; the more\n   specific wins on conflict. Three and four firing at once is the normal case, not an\n   edge case.\n5. **Nothing fires → `AGENTS.md` alone governs.** Do not hunt for a rule to apply.\n\n### Precedence\n\n| Level | Source | Can be overridden? |\n|-------|--------|--------------------|\n| 1 | Every `AGENTS.md` §1 hard blocker, the Four Laws, PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK, Comment Hygiene, and every mandatory gate in §2 | No |\n| 2 | An explicit, in-the-moment operator instruction | Not applicable, it is the instruction |\n| 3 | These rule files, and the guidance in a skill's `SKILL.md` | Only by level 1 or 2 |\n| 4 | General judgment | By anything above |\n\nA rule file may tighten `AGENTS.md`. None relaxes a HARD BLOCK or authorizes what\n`AGENTS.md` forbids. Gate 5 does not change that: it makes the **load** mandatory,\nwhile what you load stays at level 3, the obligation to read is tier 1, the content\nis not.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TRIGGER TABLE\n\n| You are about to… | Load | It settles |\n|-------------------|------|-----------|\n| Add a file, module, class, interface, option, layer, or dependency · write a spec or plan that adds one · generalize something that works · write \"flexible\", \"future-proof\", \"scalable\", \"extensible\", \"might need\", \"best practice\", \"while we're here\" · add a test beyond the coverage floor | [`prevent-overengineering.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Whether this should exist at all, and at what size |\n| Touch a file outside the ask · fix something noticed in passing · change something else because it would make the fix easier · rename, reformat, or delete beyond the named area · deviate from an approved plan · decide what to do with the rest when part of the work is blocked · notice a defect, smell or stale comment outside the files in scope | [`scope-discipline.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | What is yours to change, and how to raise what isn't |\n| Say \"done\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", \"no regressions\" · report a result · quote a number · act on a tool's or sub-agent's success report · close out a turn · report a file path or command output · write a completion summary or tick something off as done | [`evidence-and-proof.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | What counts as proof, how a green run lies, what an honest close-out contains |\n| Decide whether to hand work to another runtime at all · hand it to a CLI executor, sub-agent, fan-out lineage, or deep loop · compose the prompt one will act on · accept or quote what one returned · answer a judgment question from your own reading alone | [`delegation-and-orchestration.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | The orchestrating posture, what a brief must carry, why one model is one opinion |\n| Delete, overwrite, migrate, deploy, publish, send, install · force-push or rewrite history · change a shared contract · touch auth, data, or config · make any call that leaves this machine · truncate · touch branches, tags, or reflogs | [`blast-radius.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Reversibility, the rollback sentence, when to stop for a yes |\n| Diagnose a failure · make a red check green · attempt the same fix twice · add a special case, retry, sleep, or broadened catch · call a failure a flake, infra, or pre-existing | [`root-cause-and-debugging.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fixing the producer instead of the symptom, and when to level up to the seam |\n| Answer without certainty · contradict the operator · fill a gap with a plausible guess · hit a contradiction between two things that must both be true · name a path, flag, function, version, or number you have not verified · not know while a plausible answer is available · see sources disagree, or the code contradict the spec, the docs or the operator · the operator asserts something you believe is wrong · change a checked answer after pushback or doubt, or drop an approach before it concludes · cite a rule, restriction, policy, limit or permission, or decline a request | [`uncertainty-and-honesty.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Confidence bands, UNKNOWN, contradiction halts |\n| Write any substantive reply, an answer, an explanation, a close-out or a status · draft or edit any sentence a reader will read · present a recommendation, a fork, or a trade-off · start a multi-step stretch of work the reader will not see inside · report what a long autonomous run found · the reader says they did not follow or asks for a plainer version | [`communication.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | How a reply reads: answer first, one recommended path, length, filler, plain sentences, punctuation, and no table in a reply |\n| End a turn · report work done, blocked, or partly done · end a turn while something you started is still running · ask the operator anything · end a turn on a fork or two acceptable paths · continue past a decision nobody made | [`communication-handoff.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | What is the operator's to do next, what is still running and what resumes it, and when a question becomes a structured choice |\n| Wire, rewire or remove a mode in a parent-hub skill · edit a hub's registry, router, root `ROUTER.md`, `graph-metadata.json` or `SKILL.md` mode table, or a mode packet's own `ROUTER.md` · report that a mode is registered, routed, reachable or integrated · quote a per-hub gate result · create a new skill under a hub, or refactor one that already lives there | [`skill-hub-routing.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | The two routing stages, what \"integrated\" requires, and checking the hub you actually changed |\n\n---\n\n## 3. INDEX\n\n| Rule | Summary |\n|------|---------|\n| [Overengineering](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Build the smallest thing that solves the stated problem; take a costlier move only by naming what fails at the cheaper one. |\n| [Scope discipline](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | The requested scope is the deliverable. Adjacent problems get named, not fixed. |\n| [Evidence and proof](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred. |\n| [Delegation and orchestration](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | Delegating makes you the orchestrator; brief with evidence, and no single model's verdict closes a question. |\n--- target exists?\nls: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts: No such file or directory\n--- hooks README\n---\ntitle: \"Skill Advisor Hook Tests\"\ndescription: \"Regression coverage for settings-driven skill advisor hook invocation shape.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"skill advisor hook tests\"\n  - \"settings driven invocation parity\"\n---\n\n# Skill Advisor Hook Tests\n\n> Regression coverage for settings-driven skill advisor hook invocation shape.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`tests/hooks/` guards the checked-in Claude settings shape used by skill advisor hook invocation.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Confirms each hook event uses the nested matcher-group shape.\n- Ensures hook commands point at `dist/hooks/claude/*` handlers.\n- Blocks accidental `hooks/copilot/` adapter references in Claude settings.\n\n---\n\n## 2. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n```text\nhooks/\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"ls -1 \\\"REPO RULES.md\\\" 2>/dev/null && head -60 \\\"REPO RULES.md\\\"; echo \\\"--- target exists?\\\"; ls -l .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts 2>&1; echo \\\"--- hooks README\\\"; head -30 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/README.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794532226545,"end":1794532227690}}}}
