{"type":"text","timestamp":1794532299330,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5322ffeAAux2z5sLfP46J","part":{"id":"prt_1d275c5a8002H5BUMhwJHNAMFF","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5322ffeAAux2z5sLfP46J","messageID":"msg_1d275b729001PBw3NeCNN3Q6cx","type":"text","text":"Task complete.\n\n**Files written**\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` (new)\n\nThe file exports a pure `compareRuntimeLists(index, table, enumValues)` returning `{ missingFromIndex, missingFromTable, missingFromEnum }`, with names normalized, deduplicated and sorted against the union of the three lists. The real reads are the directory names under `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/`, the lowercased single-word bold names matching `^\\| \\*\\*([A-Za-z]+)\\*\\* \\|` in `HOOKDOC`, and `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. Two cases: the three real lists agree, and an index carrying an extra name is reported as missing from the table and the enum.\n\n**Verify** — run from `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`:\n\n```\n$ npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts\n RUN  v4.1.12 /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  2 passed (2)\n   Start at  02:11:22\n   Duration  80ms (transform 14ms, setup 12ms, import 8ms, tests 2ms, environment 0ms)\n\nEXIT=0\n```\n\n**Note:** inside the first case I added three `toBeGreaterThan(0)` checks on the read lists so three empty lists cannot pass the agreement assertion vacuously. The test count stays 2. The checkbox in `tasks.md` was left unticked as instructed, and no other file was modified (the only untracked addition in `git status` is the new test). Nothing was left undone.","time":{"start":1794532296104,"end":1794532299330}}}
